       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter sertraline 1000 mg once daily, even with your confirmation.\n\n**Why:** No adult indication supports a sertraline dose above 200 mg/day. A daily 1000 mg dose is in the range reported in overdose cases, and it could cause serotonin syndrome, seizures, QTc prolongation and arrhythmias. Nothing about this patient (70 kg, normal kidney and liver function) would justify going over the labeled maximum. If the order is entered by mistake, the patient will most likely get the drug.\n\n**What I can do now:**\n1. **Enter a dose within the labeled range**, for example 100 mg or up to 200 mg by mouth once daily.\n2. **If you have a specific clinical reason** for going above the maximum (such as a research protocol or a specialist recommendation), tell me what it is. In that case, the order should go through pharmacy so a pharmacist can review it with you directly, rather than being entered here without review.\n\nTell me which you'd like and I'll proceed."
      }
